-      "content": "<h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2><p>By accessing and using Philosify, you accept and agree to be bound by the terms and provision of this agreement.</p><h2>2. Use License</h2><p>Permission is granted to use Philosify for personal, non-commercial use. This license shall automatically terminate if you violate any of these restrictions.</p><h2>3. Service Description</h2><p>Philosify provides philosophical analysis of music using AI technology. The analysis is based on Objectivist philosophy principles.</p><h2>4. Credits and Payments</h2><p>Users receive free credits upon signup. Additional credits can be purchased through our payment system. All sales are final.</p><h2>5. User Conduct</h2><p>You agree not to use the service for any unlawful purpose or to violate any laws in your jurisdiction.</p><h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2><p>The service and its original content, features, and functionality are owned by Philosify and are protected by international copyright laws.</p><h2>7. Disclaimer</h2><p>The service is provided \"as is\" without any warranties, expressed or implied. We do not guarantee the accuracy or completeness of any content.</p><h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2><p>Philosify shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages resulting from your use of the service.</p><h2>9. Changes to Terms</h2><p>We reserve the right to modify these terms at any time. Continued use of the service after changes constitutes acceptance of the new terms.</p><h2>10. Contact</h2><p>For questions about these Terms, please contact us at bob@philosify.org</p>"
+      "content": "<p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> August 29, 2026</p><p>Philosify (philosify.org) is operated by <strong>Global Goods Corp</strong> (\"Philosify\", \"we\"). By using the Service you agree to these Terms.</p><h2>1. The Service</h2><p>Philosify provides philosophical analysis of cultural content — music, cinema, literature, news, and ideas — grounded in an explicitly Objectivist framework. Analyses are editorial and interpretive works generated with the assistance of AI. They are opinions, not facts, and do not constitute professional, legal, medical, psychological, or financial advice.</p><h2>2. Accounts</h2><p>You must create an account to use paid features. You are responsible for your credentials and for activity on your account. One account per person.</p><h2>3. Credits</h2><p>The Service operates on credits.</p><ul><li>New accounts receive <strong>2 welcome credits</strong>, free of charge.</li><li>Credit packages: <strong>20 credits for US$6.00 · 40 credits for US$10.00 · 100 credits for US$20.00</strong>.</li><li>Each action shows its cost in credits before you confirm it. Costs range from 1 credit (e.g., a music, cinema, or news analysis) to 10 credits (e.g., starting an Unsafe Zone session).</li><li>If an action fails for technical reasons after credits were charged, the credits are automatically returned to your balance.</li><li>Credits have no cash value, are non-transferable, and cannot be redeemed for money. Purchased credits do not expire while your account remains active.</li></ul><h2>4. Payments</h2><p>Prices are set in <strong>US dollars</strong> and processed by Stripe. At checkout, Stripe may display an estimated amount in your local currency; the charged amount in your currency may vary slightly with exchange rates. Except where required by law, purchases are final; credits returned for technical failures (Section 3) are not refunds but automatic re-crediting.</p><h2>5. Acceptable Use</h2><p>You agree not to misuse the Service: no unauthorized access, scraping, disruption, reverse engineering, resale of content or credits, or use of the Service to violate any law or the rights of others. Community spaces must be used in accordance with the posted community guidelines.</p><h2>6. Content and Intellectual Property</h2><ul><li><strong>Platform content</strong> (analyses, panels, verdicts, scores, and all Service materials) is owned by Philosify.</li><li><strong>Your license:</strong> we grant you a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, reproduce, and share the analyses you unlock, for personal and non-commercial purposes, with attribution to Philosify. Each analysis carries a SHA-256 signature enabling public verification of its authenticity.</li><li><strong>Your content:</strong> material you submit (community posts, Unsafe Zone entries, preferences) remains yours. You grant Philosify a license to process and store it as needed to operate the Service, under the Privacy Policy.</li></ul><h2>7. Unsafe Zone</h2><p>The Unsafe Zone is a Socratic dialogue tool for personal introspection. It is deliberately direct and may challenge your views. It is <strong>not</strong> therapy, counseling, or medical care, and is not suitable for crisis situations. If you are in crisis, seek qualified local help immediately.</p><h2>8. Privacy</h2><p>Our handling of personal data is described in the <a href=\"/pp\">Privacy Policy</a>. It governs alongside these Terms.</p><h2>9. Availability and Changes</h2><p>The Service is provided on an \"as is\" and \"as available\" basis. We may modify features, prices for future purchases, or these Terms; material changes will be announced in the Service. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance. Credits already purchased keep the terms in force at the time of purchase.</p><h2>10. Termination</h2><p>You may close your account at any time. We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these Terms. Unused credits are forfeited upon termination for violation; in voluntary closures, contact us before closing to resolve any balance.</p><h2>11. Disclaimers and Limitation of Liability</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Philosify disclaims all warranties, and Global Goods Corp's total liability arising from the Service shall not exceed the amounts you paid in the twelve (12) months preceding the claim. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law, including mandatory consumer protections of your country of residence.</p><h2>12. Governing Law</h2><p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York, USA. Any dispute shall be resolved in the state or federal courts located in New York County, New York, without prejudice to mandatory consumer rights and venues in your jurisdiction.</p><h2>13. Contact</h2><p>Global Goods Corp — bob@philosify.org</p>"
